    {
      "section": "Introduction",
      "text": "A **DeepSeek Harness plugin** for the GitHub Trending board: it schedules daily / weekly / monthly digests, hands them to the local [`trendradar`](https://github.com/morehao/trendradar) core to scrape Trending, write Chinese intros and period summaries, and commits the result to your own repository with a PR merged automatically. You follow status, read digests and manage subscriptions from the workbench — no command line needed."
    },
    {
      "section": "Positioning",
      "text": "- **An entry point, not an engine**. Scraping, parsing, model summarization, rendering, git and PR all live in one place — the local `trendradar` core. The plugin only handles **configuration, scheduling, spawning the core and displaying results**, so there is no second implementation to drift.\n- **Deliver the artifact as-is**. Content is written byte-for-byte exactly as the core produces it; the plugin does not rewrite, reorder or re-invoke a model on it.\n- **Local execution, no telemetry**. The core runs on your machine; the plugin has no cloud account, and secrets are handed to the core only over a runtime channel — never written to config files or logs."
    },
